    <string name="fix_module_title">Generate fix module</string>
    <string name="fix_module_msg">A zip named cubclone-sdcardfs-fix.zip will be written to the Download folder (an existing one is overwritten). Flash it in APatch / KernelSU / Magisk and reboot.\n\nThe module does two things:\n1. Switches external storage to pure FUSE mounting — with sdcardfs in the kernel a clone volume cannot be mounted at all, which is the root cause;\n2. On pure FUSE every read and write is proxied by the system media provider, which cannot modify files left over from the sdcardfs era; apps then fail to open their own databases (import errors, 0-byte exports, endless loading). Once the device is unlocked the module re-owns those legacy files to the local media provider — owner only, no change to content or location, runs once and leaves a marker.\n\nDevices whose kernel has no sdcardfs are rejected at install time and nothing is left behind.\n\nNote: ROM OTA updates usually require re-flashing the module.</string>
